A||||11||Songman||88 trouble (again!)||||1||
Z||000000||Songman||12-26-2000||04:59 PM||||Well, I made my way over to Ed Park's Fiero Factory this weekend with the 88 Formula that I am trading to Doug for the Indy. Man! It was great to see all the Fieros Ed has!<P>Now for the bad news... As I was on my way back from GA after visiting my family for the holiday, the 88 coupe that I just replaced the complete ignition system in just died!<P>Seventy miles per hour down the interstate and it just died! Almost mid-night. Middle of nowhere. From the smell of it, it is still getting gas so I figure some of those new ignition parts must have failed. Still trying to get a tow truck to get it off of the side of the interstate. Will probably work on it tomorrow. Anyone have any ideas or suggestions? I think it is probably the module since it just died all at once. Still turns over great, but doesn't hit at all...<P>And I just have to give praise to the good people in the world... A guy who was on his way from Florida to St Louis stopped to offer assistance and when nothing could be done gave me and my girlfriend a ride home! Believe me, at midnight on Christmas with the temperature around 30 degrees, this guy did a very good deed!||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||12-26-2000||05:05 PM||||Well if you didn't think of it already I am going to say check your fuses.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ronnie||12-26-2000||05:21 PM||||That's exactly how mine died about 2 weeks ago!! First check all the fuses as mentioned. Then , check to see if the rotor is turning while cranking! Turned out , mine was a broke timing chain!!!! You can also look inside the oil fill cap to see if the rockers are moving while a helper is cranking the engine over.No movement, no timing chain!!! Just mine back this week.||||reg||6
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-26-2000||06:11 PM||||Since it's an '88 coupe it doesn't have a rotor or timing chain (DIS ignition and timing gears) I would have to agree with your self assessment......it's likely the ignition module or coil packs.  What brand did you use?  <P>I would probably carry a spare module/coil packs with me from now on.....just in case.<P>If the car is relatively close to the Fiero Factory give Ed a call and have him tow it back to the shop. I'm sure Jeremy and Dave can fix whatever is wrong with it.<P><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 12-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||12-26-2000||07:41 PM||||Besides recently joining Triple-A, the possibility of being stranded on the road prompted me to search & print the F.O.L.D. list of owners in my area, and I keep that list in the car (have a cellphone of course).  If I take a trip in my Fiero, I'll print a list for the locations where I go.  FOLD has some old data, but if we all keep our information up to date it can be a great service.<BR>- <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/cgi-local/foldinstructions.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/cgi-local/foldinstructions.htm</A> <P> ||||reg||6
Z||000005||theogre||12-26-2000||08:50 PM||||Read the cave article on DIS. Make sure that sheild is not missing.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||12-26-2000||09:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>Well if you didn't think of it already I am going to say check your fuses.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Is this the regular fuses under the dash (or wherever they are in a Fiero)? I have never had a reason to even look for fuses. I will check that as soon as I get the thing home.<P>Thanks to everyone for responding. As soon as I get it home I will know more and let you know what it turns out to be.<P>Also, it is good to know about the FOLD thing. Never even heard of it but I am now signed up! Great idea!<P>Headed over to Ogre's Cave now to read more about DIS.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Songman||12-26-2000||09:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>Read the cave article on DIS. Make sure that sheild is not missing.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Okay Ogre...<BR>I just read your notes on the DIS and shielding. I am not sure if I moved any metal plate to the new module or not. <P>Let's say I didn't.... Did I likely mess anything up or do I just need to get the metal plate and put it in?<P>And now let's say I did... Assuming that there are no blown fuses or anything like that...the module or the crank sensor are still the most likely culprits since it will not fire at all, aren't they?<P>Thanks.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||12-27-2000||10:27 PM||||Finally got the coupe home this evening! Had to borrow a tow dolly from a friend. The worst thing was that no one was available to help so I had to push the thing up onto the dolly by myself! Who knew these little cars weighed so much?!?<P>Guess I'll start checking things out tomorrow. For now I am going to relax. <P>Also, have to take that big stupid red label off of the window that the Tennessee State Patrol put on there for me! The car had only been there for 6 hours when they did that! I see cars that sit for days and are never tagged!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Black88GT||12-27-2000||11:58 PM||||Songman, ask Mike (hyptnotise), me, and some good samaratin how hard it is to push an 88 Coupe up a slight hill in the middle of the night....<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||11
Z||000010||Songman||12-28-2000||05:27 PM||||I imagine it would be even harder with a V6!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Songman||12-29-2000||09:06 PM||||Haven't braved the snow to get out there and take the module off yet, but I was over at Advance Auto Parts today where I bought the module a few months ago.... He said that he could test the module for me, and luckily, I bought the lifetime warranty one! Now I guess I just need to start hunting for the DIS shield plate that Ogre told me about, juts in case I didn't transfer it over...||||reg||10
